  Quote of the Week:

  Pope Julius II, in reply to Michelangelo, who had asked which of his 
artistic tools the Pope would like to try (1506):
  "Nay, give me a sword, for I am no scholar."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  Winter melted into spring, and Piotr prepared to carry out his urgent 
assignments.  He prepared his armies to defend Archangel and the surrounding 
provinces.
  Kitralus returned to Valhalla, having done his best to fulfill his 
assignments.


  Thus endeth the adventures of Piotr the Magnificent for this year.



  Here is the financial report for Piotr's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 0 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  0 
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Piotr was left with 18 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Tattoo, Squire to Indra
To: Piotr

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter gave way to sweet spring.  Indra prepared her forces to defend 
Copenhagen and the surrounding provinces.

  Thy humble servant,   Tattoo, Squire to Indra


From: Kitralus
To: Piotr

  Honored Sovereign, 

  I returned to Valhalla, having done my best to fulfill my assignments.


  Thy humble servant,   Kitralus


